      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Lot 2 Derelict residence on approx. 3.1 acres (1.26 ha)\n\n• Derelict residence with potential to create superb residential holding (subject to planning permission)\n• Excellent location close to M1 motorway, Balbriggan town and train station and approx. 15 minutes drive to the M50\n• Significant road frontage\n• Suitable for any agricultural or equestrian purposes\n\nM1 motorway 1km, Balbriggan 2km, Dublin Airport 22km\n\nGuide Price:\nPrice on Application\n\nType of Transaction\nFor sale by Online Auction via Coonan.com on Friday 25th September at 4.15pm\n\nLocation\nThis fine property is situated to the southwest of the popular commuter town of Balbriggan in north Co. Dublin. This property sits in an area of quality farmland and one-off housing while also benefiting from it`s close proximity to the M1 motorway at Junction 6.\n\nBalbriggan provides all local amenities and the town centre and harbour area are being reshaped through the \"Our Balbriggan\" regeneration initiative. Balbriggan itself has grown steadily in recent years, with strong residential and commercial development. The popular commuter town has excellent transport links including a train station on the Belfast Dublin line as well as regular bus services to Dublin city and surrounds.\n\nSolicitors:\nMr. Eoin Thomas McGuiness of AMOSS, Warrington House, Mount Street Cresent, Dublin 2. T: 01 212 0400\n\nViewing:\nBy appointment at any reasonable hour.\n\nDirections:\nEircode: K32 FY86\n\nContact Information\nPhilip Byrne\n01 628 6128\nphilipb@coonan.com"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Notice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
